IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art01-definitions`

-- je21-part4-office: Article 22 (Privilege) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
-- The rest of Part 4, Articles 19 to 21 and 23, is in the coverage table of NOTES.md:
-- it renames and organises an office and sets its officer's functions and delegations, none of which a reader of an enactment can ask a question of.
--
-- Article 22(1) gives legal professional privilege to "confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter".
-- Article 22(2) says what "confidential communications" and "provider of instructions" include; both say "includes", and the model does not read them as complete.
-- What the privilege consists of (who may waive it, and what follows from it in proceedings) the Law does not say, and the model does not add it.
--
-- Article 1 defines "Legislative Drafter" "unless the context indicates otherwise".
-- The model takes it that Article 22(1) uses the term as Article 1 defines it, and passes FALSE for the context.

§ `Article 22 -- Privilege`

§§ `22(2) The people and the communications the Article names`

-- Answers: is this person a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office?
-- A Member of the States, an officer working in a department established by the States, and an officer working in a body, office or unit of administration established on behalf of the States, are.
-- "includes" leaves room for others, who give instructions to the Office; the reader states that last fact.
-- src:213 | “provider of instructions” includes a Member of the States and any officer working in –
-- src:214 | (a) a department established by the States; or
-- src:215 | (b) a body, office or unit of administration, established on behalf of the States (including under any legislation).
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 22(2) "provider of instructions" (src:213-215)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a provider of instructions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 22(2): the person is a provider of instructions` person MEANS
        person's `is a Member of the States`
    OR  person's `is an officer working in a department established by the States`
    OR  person's `is an officer working in a body, office or unit of administration established on behalf of the States`
    OR  person's `otherwise provides instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office`

-- Answers: is this communication a confidential communication within Article 22?
-- Instructions to draft legislation, communications between a client and a Legislative Drafter about the subject matter of the instructions, and unpublished drafts, are.
-- Any other communication is one only if it is confidential in fact, which the reader states.
-- src:210 | “confidential communications” includes –
-- src:211 | (a) instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office and communications between any client of the Legislative Drafting Office and any Legislative Drafter that relate to the subject matter of the instructions;
-- src:212 | (b) unpublished drafts of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 22(2) "confidential communications" (src:210-212)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of communication under Article 22`
      `the communication is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 22(2): the communication is a confidential communication` kind `the communication is confidential` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `instructions to draft legislation received by the Legislative Drafting Office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a communication between a client of the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter that relates to the subject matter of the instructions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an unpublished draft of legislation prepared by or on behalf of the Legislative Drafting Office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other communication` THEN `the communication is confidential`

§§ `22(1) The privilege`

-- Answers: is this communication subject to legal professional privilege by Article 22(1)?
-- It is if it is a confidential communication between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter.
-- FALSE means Article 22(1) does not give the privilege; whether the communication is privileged on some other footing the Article does not say.
-- src:208 | (1) Confidential communications between a provider of instructions to the Legislative Drafting Office and a Legislative Drafter are subject to legal professional privilege.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 22(1) (src:208)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a provider of instructions`
      `the other party's role` IS A `Role in the Legislative Drafting Office`
      kind IS A `Kind of communication under Article 22`
      `the communication is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 22(1): the communication is subject to legal professional privilege` person `the other party's role` kind `the communication is confidential` MEANS
        `Article 22(2): the person is a provider of instructions` person
    AND `Article 1 "Legislative Drafter": the person is a Legislative Drafter` `the other party's role` FALSE
    AND `Article 22(2): the communication is a confidential communication` kind `the communication is confidential`
